e i have brought here into the whiteboard so in this figure we have uh model predictions and we have ground truth right so three tokens are predicted for every ground truth so if the ground truth is one the next three tokens are two three four the actual next tokens is two when the input is two the next tokens predicted are three four five but the actual next token is three when the input token is three the next tokens which are predicted by the model are four five and a and the actual token is four when the actual token is four the next predicted tokens are five a and b but the actual next token is five when the input is five the next three tokens predicted are a b and c and the actual token is a similarly when a is the actual token or a is the input token b is the next token etc now if you look at the ground truth can you identify that point which can be which can be classified as a choice point what is that key token which significantly influences future outcomes so you can pause the video for a moment here and answer this question what is the key token here in this ground truth sequence in this ground truth sequence which significantly influences or impacts the future outcomes so one gives two two gives three four gives five that much is fine and a gives b that is also fine but the key token here which actually can be called as a choice point is this five leads to a right because it''s at this point where a complete transition happens we are predicting numbers initially sequentially and then suddenly go from predicting numbers to predicting alphabets so this is a key point or this is a choice point okay now what i want to mention is that uh please keep in mind among all of these predictions there is there are multiple places in which token a is actually coming so three right when three is the input token although the correct answer is four for the next token our model also produces a as one of the future tokens when five is the input token our model also sorry when four is the input token our model here also produces a and when five is the input token of course the model produces a right so what i want to point out here is that token a is actually a part of multiple predictions right it appears in the prediction starting from let me change the color here it appears in the predictions of three four as well as five so errors which are related to predicting a appear repeatedly in the loss calculation so as we''ll see tomorrow when we define the loss function the loss function for every input token consists of all of its predicted tokens so the loss function now consists a here it consists of a here it consists of a over here so the errors related to predicting a appear repeatedly in the loss calculation right uh hence the loss function is the over here it consists of all of its predicted tokens so the loss function is the over here and hence the training process implicitly prioritizes improving predictions of such consequential tokens focusing the model''s capacity on more critical decisions rather than inconsequential ones now in the overall loss of the language model in the multi-token prediction the prediction of the token a will have a much higher weightage much higher multiple times it does not just come up when 5 is the input this token a actually comes up when 3 is the input when 4 is the input etc so it plays a big role in the overall loss calculation and here again the multi-token prediction loss hence assigns higher implicit weights to consequential tokens so a is a consequential token now right and when we look at the multi-token prediction loss tomorrow we are going to see that the multi-token prediction loss implicitly assigns a higher weight to these consequential tokens and what this means is that now we just get better at planning into the future right especially for such choice for such choice points the model learns to prioritize crucial decision making elements which are very important so in this particular