 up to three times faster inference speed and this is also mentioned in the uh this is also mentioned in the paper actually the paper talks a lot about uh training as well as they talk about inference so if you see section 3.2 it''s called faster inference and they observe speed up of three times on code with an average of 2.5 accepted tokens out of three suggestions on code so it just means that uh inference actually becomes much faster with multi-token prediction now whenever you uh see about multi-token prediction right you''ll also hear this term which is called a self-speculative decoding and it comes under the domain of inference right so in self-speculative decoding what is actually done is that if you look at the left hand side during inference only one token is predicted at a time but in self-speculative decoding we predict multiple tokens at a time which means multiple tokens are inferred at a single time through a language model and then another larger language model is used to verify those responses if they are correct though those are retained if they are wrong those are not retained so this is called as parallel verification and this idea is called a speculative decoding which speeds up llm inference now multi-token prediction makes speculative decoding possible because in speculative decoding we are considering multiple inferred tokens at once right and multi-token prediction is exactly built for this through multi-token prediction we can predict multiple new tokens at a given time right and that''s why multi-token prediction is often associated with speeding up llm inference and also with self-speculative or speculative decoding so as i mentioned speculative decoding involves two models it involves a small language model which quickly predicts the next k tokens in a sequence now here is where multi-token prediction is used and it also uses a main large language model which verifies the tokens generated by the draft model and corrects them as needed so that''s why you will see the word here self-speculative decoding which is used during inference okay the reason i''m mentioning all of these terminologies to you and providing a quick intuition is because when you hear the term multi-token prediction you''ll often hear the terms densification of training signal then you will hear they''re better at planning then you will hear the term sense speculative decoding so you should have a basic idea of what these terminologies mean so in summary the four main reasons why multi-token prediction is useful is that it leads to densification of training signals which means that the training just becomes a lot more richer as we saw the key thing to note here is that in single token prediction the model only learns images immediate next step dependencies with multi-token prediction the model sees and learns the relationship across multiple future steps simultaneously and thus it develops better representations with respect to planning and forecasting that''s the first reason which we saw densification of training signals second reason is improved data efficiency so this is a quantified result which has been proved in this paper where they show that on the mbpp and human eval benchmark multi-token prediction consistently outperforms single token prediction the third result or the third reason why multi-token prediction is useful is better planning and here we saw we saw this in a very intuitive manner that multi-token prediction implicitly assigns higher importance to choice point and a choice point is that point which leads to consequential uh next tokens so multi-token prediction loss assigns higher higher implicit weights to consequential tokens and it assigns lower implicit weights to individual tokens and that''s why multi-token prediction is useful in consequential tokens that''s why it''s better at planning and the fourth reason which we saw is it has a higher inference speed up to three times uh faster in inference speed and if you want to implement speculative decoding you need two language models right you can use a small language model which predicts the next k tokens in a sequence you can use multi-token prediction for this and you can use a larger language model to verify the token generated by this small model which is also called as the draft model okay so these are the four main reasons why multi-token prediction is actually useful and now the last thing which i want to mention today briefly is that deep seek used multi-token prediction gains only during pre-training okay so during inference they did not use speculative decoding they only used multi-token prediction during pre-training because of multiple reasons because they got densification of training signals because of improved data efficiency because of improved planning etc but they did not use the higher inference speed of multi-token prediction in fact during inference they only predicted one single token at a time and this is mentioned in their paper over here our mtp strategy multi-token prediction strategy only mainly aims to improve the performance of the main model so during the inference we can directly discard the mtp modules and the main model can function independently and normally additionally we can also repurpose these mtp modules for speculative decoding so they have said we can also repurpose this multi-token prediction models for speculative decoding they have not done it but they said that we can do it but the main version 3 paper used a single token prediction for inference so during inference they discarded the mtp modules and as they are mentioned at the start an mtp objective densifies the training signals we have already seen what densification of training signal means and here they also say it may improve data efficiency we have already seen what these this mean so the reason i have covered this point number one and point number two here densification of training signals and improve data efficiency it''s because it''s directly mentioned in the deep seek paper here they have also mentioned mtp may enable the model to pre-plan its representations for better prediction of future tokens and we have seen this also here we saw that in the densification the multi-token prediction guides internal representations towards better planning and we also saw that planning is improved in this better planning section where we saw that the model the multi-token prediction implicitly assigns greater importance to choice points and thus it''s good at decision making into the future so all of these points which have been mentioned in the deep seek first paragraph usually when you read it you feel that you''ve understood it right but beneath it there is a lot of intuition and theory which i wanted to explain in today''s lecture in in the next lecture on multi-token prediction we''ll understand the multi-token prediction modules so especially we''ll understand the exact mathematics behind how multi-token prediction is implemented by deep seek so i''ve written all of this on the whiteboard which we are going to go through sequentially and finally we are going to code a multi-token prediction module fully from scratch all right so i hope all of you found today''s lecture useful informative and intuitive the main idea behind today''s lecture was to give you an intuition behind why multi-token prediction is used by deep seek and i believe many modern llms might start using multi-token prediction so i hope you are excited for the next lectures which involve mtp or multi-token prediction mathematics and then coding it from there so thank you very much for watching and i will see you in the next lecture. as i''m making these lectures it''s important that all of you make notes along with me because multi multi-relatant attention and mixture of experts were challenging concepts multi-token prediction is not as challenging but it''s still important that these three fundamental building 